# Axtrizen AI — Feature Roadmap & Priority Plan

> Based on deep research into 30+ AI coding tools (Devin, Manus, Cursor, Windsurf, VSCode Agent, etc.), 3000+ OpenClaw community skills, and your current codebase state.

---

## Current State Summary

Your app already has a solid foundation with these **working features**:
- ✅ Application shell (Tauri 2.0, dark theme, collapsible sidebar)
- ✅ Dashboard (live metrics, gateway health, cost tracking)
- ✅ Agent CRUD (create, list, settings, delete, status)
- ✅ Chat (1:1, send/receive, markdown, history)
- ✅ Teams (create, add/remove members, group chat with @tag orchestration)
- ✅ Projects (create, workspace generation, details, delete)
- ✅ Settings (theme, gateway URL, debug mode)
- ✅ Global search, notifications, user profile

---

## 🔴 Tier 1: Critical Must-Have Features (Immediate Priority)

These are the features that make Axtrizen a *functioning* autonomous SDLC platform rather than just a management UI. Without these, the core value proposition doesn't work.

### 1. SDLC Execution Engine (The Core Differentiator)

**Why it matters:** This is what separates Axtrizen from every other AI tool. Devin runs a single agent loop; Manus has a planner module + knowledge module. Axtrizen's multi-agent SDLC is unique.

| Sub-Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **Phase Orchestration** | Manager agent drives 4 phases: Planning → Design → Development → Testing. Each phase triggers specific agent behaviors | 8 pts |
| **Plan Generation & Parsing** | Manager generates project plan as structured JSON (epics → stories → tasks). Auto-parsed and stored in DB | 5 pts |
| **Task Assignment Engine** | Manager assigns tasks to worker agents based on role/capability. Tasks appear on the Kanban board | 5 pts |
| **Code File Extraction** | Parse agent responses for code blocks, extract filenames, save as real files in workspace directory | 5 pts |
| **Revision Loop** | Manager reviews each agent's work. Up to 2 rounds of revision before accepting | 3 pts |
| **Human Feedback Gate** | Pause execution between phases. Human approves/revises before proceeding | 3 pts |
| **Final Deliverables Report** | Generate `FINAL_REPORT.md` at completion: what was built, files created, how to run, next steps | 3 pts |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is the #1 priority. The entire product's value depends on this engine working end-to-end.

---

### 2. Project Board (Kanban + List View)

**Why it matters:** Users need to *see* what the agents are doing. Every competitor (Devin, Manus) provides progress visibility. Your board is the Jira-equivalent for AI work.

| Sub-Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **Kanban View** | 5 columns: Backlog → Todo → In Progress → Review → Done. Cards show task title, assignee, priority | 5 pts |
| **List/Tree View** | Hierarchical: Epic → Story → Task with expandable rows and progress bars | 5 pts |
| **Real-Time Refresh** | Auto-refresh every 5 seconds + immediate refresh on `project-plan-ready` event | 2 pts |
| **Progress Bars** | Per-epic completion percentage: [(doneTasks / totalTasks) * 100](file:///Users/akashranjan/Desktop/openclaw/research/maple-oss/maple/state/store.py#156-214) | 2 pts |
| **Sprint Filtering** | Filter board by sprint iteration | 2 pts |

---

### 3. Agent-to-Agent Communication Protocol (via Maple OSS)

**Why it matters:** Manus has an event stream for inter-module communication. Devin uses planning mode for coordination. Your agents need a structured way to talk to each other within a team. We will integrate **[Maple OSS](https://github.com/maheshvaikri-code/maple-oss)** directly into the OpenClaw Python environment to handle this natively.

| Sub-Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **Maple Broker Setup** | Deploy NATS or use Maple's memory broker for agent pub/sub communication | 3 pts |
| **P2P Task Delegation** | Manager agent uses Maple `ResourceRequest` to assign tasks to workers based on capacity | 5 pts |
| **Secure Review Protocol** | Use Maple's LIM (Link Identification Mechanism) for secure Dev ↔ QA code review loops | 3 pts |
| **Distributed State Sync** | Use Maple's `StateManager` to keep all team agents aware of the current project phase | 3 pts |

---

## 🟡 Tier 2: High-Value Features (Next Sprint)

These features significantly improve the user experience and make the platform feel professional.

### 4. Workspace File Browser & Code Viewer

**Why it matters:** Devin has a full file editor. Cursor gives you code-level access. Users need to see what the agents produced, not just read chat messages.

| Sub-Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **File Tree Browser** | Display project workspace directory as a file tree with icons for file types | 3 pts |
| **Code Preview** | Click a file → view with syntax highlighting (using Monaco or CodeMirror) | 5 pts |
| **File Diff View** | Show what changed between revisions (agent edits) | 3 pts |
| **Download/Export** | Download individual files or entire workspace as ZIP | 2 pts |

---

### 5. Agent Role Templates & Skill System

**Why it matters:** The research shows **3,009 community-built skills** across categories like Coding Agents, Git/GitHub, DevOps, Web Dev, etc. Axtrizen should leverage this ecosystem.

| Sub-Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **Built-in Role Templates** | 10+ predefined roles: PM, Architect, Sr Developer, Jr Developer, QA Engineer, DevOps, Security Engineer, Code Reviewer, Business Analyst, Tech Lead | 3 pts |
| **Template Preview** | Preview system prompt, suggested model, and capabilities before applying | 2 pts |
| **Custom Templates** | Users save their own agent configs as reusable templates | 3 pts |
| **Skill Installation** | Install OpenClaw skills from ClawHub to extend agent capabilities (CLI integration) | 5 pts |
| **Skill Browser** | Browse/search available skills from within the app | 5 pts |

---

### 6. Mission Control (Multi-Agent Monitoring)

**Why it matters:** When 5+ agents are working simultaneously, the user needs a bird's-eye view. Inspired by Manus's event stream and Devin's planning mode visibility.

| Sub-Feature | Description | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **Agent Grid** | Visual grid of agent cards showing: avatar, name, status, current task, token count | 3 pts |
| **Activity Timeline** | Chronological log of all agent actions across the team | 5 pts |
| **Team Swim Lanes** | Parallel lanes showing which agent is working on what, simultaneously | 5 pts |
| **Cost Dashboard** | Running cost per agent, per project, with burn rate visualization | 3 pts |

